From: Altium-on-Wine kit
Subject: dwrite: cache glyph masks and bounds for stable linear transforms

Modules: dlls/dwrite
Base: wine-11.16

Direct2D redraws antialiased schematic labels as the viewport moves. The
translation affects glyph placement but FreeType does not use it when computing
the individual glyph bounds and masks. Reuse the existing per-face LRU for
these results and key them by the exact linear transform, glyph, font size
and simulation flags. Distinguish bitmap rendering modes from bounds and
advance lookups. Keep accounting for a bitmap added after its cache entry
and evict entries until there is room for the allocation.

